<%# The Show/Hide button inside a password field. Pair it with
    `data: password_visibility_data` on the enclosing `.password-field`.

    It renders the SHOW label, because the field starts hidden — the
    controller's connect() re-syncs it either way, so the server-rendered
    word is right before any JavaScript runs rather than flickering.

    A <button type="button">: inside the end-of-Verto card it sits in the same
    row as "Create my account", and a default-type button there would submit
    the form the respondent has not finished filling in. %>
<button type="button" class="password-field__toggle"
        data-action="password-visibility#toggle"
        data-password-visibility-target="button"><%= t("auth.show") %></button>
